Subject: [PATCH 0095] framebuffer: accelerated-head mode (nullmoth-fbflags 0x200) for NMXAccel's GPU compositing

The panel framebuffer as NMXAccel's head 0, following ericek111's NMXVGAFB contract (vibe-nullmoth-xe3-qemu part 4)
on the real Intel display engine, opt-in: class NMXIntelGPUFB (vendor-named for CoreDisplay's IOPresentment; the
NMXAccel built with ericek's patches + 0048 watches for it), IOFBDependentID 0x4E4D58560000001 / index 0,
IOFBMemorySize 1 GB, built-in; nvAllocVram/nvFreeVram from contiguous system memory (4 slots reserved at start);
nvScanoutInfo with the live scan-out's real physical address (stolen memory); NMXVGAFBOpen and nmxHeadOpened when
WindowServer opens it; NMXGPU's display hold kept after the publish and released by the accelerator's
nmxDisplayReady (30 s cap as before). Without 0x200 nothing changes.

